    <!-- ============ v1.8.2 Guide page ============ -->
    <string name="guide_title">How to use</string>
    <string name="guide_sec1">Start capturing · 3 steps</string>
    <string name="guide_s1_1">Open "Settings → Developer options → Wireless debugging" and keep it on</string>
    <string name="guide_s1_2">Tap the status bar on top to open the connect page; pair in split-screen: long-press this app in Recents → "Freeform" to float it, then open "Pair device with pairing code" on the main screen</string>
    <string name="guide_s1_3">Type the code shown on the main screen into the floating window → Start pairing (port auto-detected; pairing happens only once)</string>
    <string name="guide_s1_tip">Note: leaving the app or closing the dialog during pairing refreshes both the code and the port — split-screen avoids this.</string>
    <string name="guide_sec2">Split-screen pairing · illustrated</string>
    <string name="guide_img1">① Type the pairing code in the floating window (right); keep the pairing dialog open on the main screen</string>
    <string name="guide_img2">② Connected automatically after pairing; daily capture does not need pairing again</string>
    <string name="guide_sec3">Daily use (after pairing)</string>
    <string name="guide_s3_1">Turn on "Wireless debugging"</string>
    <string name="guide_s3_2">Open this app — it connects automatically and tracks port changes; no manual edits needed</string>
    <string name="guide_s3_3">After capture: ⋮ copy all / 💾 save to file</string>
    <string name="guide_s3_tip">"Wireless debugging" is just a switch: turn it off when idle and back on when needed.</string>
    <string name="guide_sec4">Capture app crashes</string>
    <string name="guide_s4_1">Switch to the "Crashes" tab and tap "Start monitoring"</string>
    <string name="guide_s4_2">Open the app that crashes and let it crash once</string>
    <string name="guide_s4_3">Back on "Crashes", records and stack traces appear automatically — copy or share them</string>
    <string name="guide_sec5">Cannot connect? Try in order</string>
    <string name="guide_s5_1">Make sure the "Wireless debugging" switch is on (the most common cause)</string>
    <string name="guide_s5_2">Tap the status bar on the home screen → Connect device → "Rescan"</string>
    <string name="guide_s5_3">Still failing: expand "Manual address" and type the IP:port from the Wireless debugging screen</string>
    <string name="guide_s5_tip">The first connection requires pairing once; after that, port changes do not need re-pairing.</string>
    <string name="guide_privacy">Note: captured logs may contain sensitive info (accounts, locations, etc.). Review before sharing.</string>

